verses.text:
Blessed is the man{a}
who does not walk in the counsel of the wicked,
nor stand in the way of sinners,
nor sit in the seat of scoffers;

The kings of the earth take their stand,
and the rulers plot together
against Yahweh and against his anointed one:{b}

I will tell of the decree:
Yahweh said to me, “You are my son;
today I have become your father.{d}

many are saying of my soul,
“There is no salvation for him in God.”
Selah{b}

Arise, Yahweh! Save me, my God!
For you have struck all my enemies on the jaw;
you have shattered the teeth of the wicked.

Salvation belongs to Yahweh;
your blessing be upon your people!
Selah

Answer me when I call, my righteous God!
When I was in trouble, you gave me room;{c}
have mercy on me and listen to my prayer.

Tremble,{f} and do not sin;
speak within your hearts on your beds, and be still.
Selah

For there is no truth in their mouth;
within them is ruin;
their throat is a grave left open;
with their tongue they speak smoothly.{e}

But let all who shelter in you be glad;
let them sing for joy forever, and cover them,
that the lovers of your name may exult in you.

I am weary with my groaning;
every night I flood my bed;
I drench my couch with my tears.

Rise up, Yahweh, in your anger;
stand tall against the rage of my enemies;
wake up on my behalf;{c} you have ordered justice.

Yahweh is the judge of the nations;
vindicate me, Yahweh, as my righteousness deserves,
and by the innocence I have.

Yahweh, our Lord,{b}
how majestic is your name in all the earth!
You have set your splendor above the heavens.{c}

Out of the mouths of children and infants
you have founded strength because of your foes,
to silence the enemy and the avenger.{d}

The enemy has come to an end in ruins forever;
you have uprooted their cities;
the very memory of them has perished.

Have mercy on me, Yahweh!
Look at how my haters make me suffer;
you raise me up from the gates of death,

that I may recount all your praises,
in the gates of the daughter of Zion{c}
I will rejoice in your salvation.

Yahweh has made himself known; he has executed judgment;
the wicked is snared in the work of his own hands.
Higgaion.{d} Selah

Put them in fear, Yahweh;
let the nations know that they are but men.
Selah

His ways are firm at all times;
your judgments are high above, out of his sight;
he scoffs at all his adversaries.

He sits in ambush near the villages;
in secret places he kills the innocent;
his eyes spy out the helpless.

He lies in wait in secret like a lion in his thicket;
he lies in wait to seize the afflicted;
he seizes the afflicted when he draws him into his net.

But you have seen it, for you observe trouble and sorrow,
and take it in hand;
the helpless entrusts himself to you;
you have always helped the orphan.

Look, the wicked draw their bows;
they have fitted their arrows to the strings
to shoot from the shadows at people with honest hearts.

Yahweh is in his holy temple;
Yahweh—his throne is in the heavens;
his eyes behold, his eyelids examine the children of man.

“Because the afflicted are plundered, because the needy groan,
now I will arise,” says Yahweh;
“I will set him in the safety for which he longs.”{a}

The words of Yahweh are pure words,
silver refined in a furnace on the ground,{b}
purified seven times.

The fool{b} has said in his heart, “There is no God.”
They act corruptly; their deeds are detestable;
not one of them does good.

All have gone astray; all alike have turned rotten;
no one does good,
no, not one.{c}

who does not slander with his tongue,
nor does evil to his companion,
nor takes up a reproach against his neighbor;

who despises those who are vile in his eyes
but gives honor to those who fear Yahweh;
who keeps his promise even when it hurts him;

who does not lend his money at interest,{a}
nor take a bribe against the innocent.
He who does these things shall never be moved.

The sorrows of those who hurry after another god shall be multiplied;
I will not pour out their drink offerings of blood,
nor take their names upon my lips.

You make me know the path of life;
with your face there is joy in full;
at your right hand, delights forever.

You have probed my heart and examined me in the night;
you have refined me and found no wrong;
I have purposed that my mouth shall not overstep.

from men by your hand, Yahweh,
from men of the world whose portion is in this life.
You fill their belly with what you have stored up;{d}
their sons are satisfied,
and they leave what remains to their little ones.

Then the earth shook and trembled;
the roots of the mountains quaked
and were shaken, for his anger blazed.

Smoke rose from his nostrils,
and fire from his mouth consumed;
coals were kindled by it.

Yahweh also thundered in the heavens,
and the Most High uttered his voice,
hailstones and coals of fire.{e}

This God—his way is blameless;
the word of Yahweh is tested;
he is a shield to all who take refuge in him.

You rescued me from the quarrels of the people;
you set me at the head of nations;
a people I did not know became my servants.

who delivers me from my enemies;
yes, you lift me up above those who rise against me;
you rescue me from the man of violence.

Yet their line goes out into all the earth,{b}
and their sayings to the farthest edge of the world.
There he has pitched a tent for the sun,

Now I know that Yahweh saves his anointed;
he will answer him from his holy heaven
with the saving might of his right hand.

My God, my God, why have you abandoned me?{b}
Why do you stay so far from helping me,
far from my cries of pain?{c}

I am poured out like water,
and all my bones are out of joint;
my heart is like wax;
it has melted within my breast.{g}

Dogs surround me;
a pack of wicked men has encircled me;
they have pierced my hands and feet.{h}

Those who fear Yahweh, praise him!
Jacob’s whole family, give him glory;
be in awe of him, every child of Israel!

The humble shall eat and be satisfied;
those who seek Yahweh shall praise him.
May your hearts live forever!

All the rich of the earth will eat and bow down;
before him will kneel everyone headed for the dust,
even the one unable to preserve his own life.{n}

He renews my life.
He leads me along straight paths{b}
because of his name.

Yes, though I walk through the valley of deep darkness,{c}
I will fear no evil, for you are beside me;
your rod and your staff are a comfort to me.

You spread a table before me
in the presence of my adversaries;
you anoint my head with oil;
my cup overflows.

Such is the generation of those who seek him,{b}
who seek your face, O God of Jacob.{c}
Selah

Lift up your heads, O you gates;
lift them up, you everlasting doors,
and the King of glory shall come in.

My God, I put my trust in you;
let me not be put to shame;
let my enemies not triumph over me.

Guide me in your truth and teach me,
for you are my saving God;
I wait for you all day.

Do not remember the sins of my youth, nor my transgressions;
remember me according to your covenant love,
for your goodness’ sake, Yahweh.

Yahweh is my light and my salvation;
whom shall I fear?
Yahweh is the stronghold of my life;
of whom shall I be afraid?

For in the day of trouble he shall hide me in his pavilion;
in the secret of his tent he shall hide me;
he shall set me up upon a rock.

Now my head will be raised above the enemies around me,
and I will offer joyful sacrifices in his tent;
I will sing and make music to Yahweh.

Hide not your face far from me;
put not your servant away in anger;
you have been my help;
leave me not, neither forsake me,
O God of my salvation.

Wait for Yahweh;
be strong, and let your heart take courage;
wait for Yahweh!

To you, Yahweh, I cry out.
My rock, do not ignore me;
if you say nothing to me,
I will become like those who descend to the pit.

Repay them for what they have done
and for their evil deeds;
repay them for the work of their hands;
give them what they deserve.

Yahweh is my strength and my shield;
I trusted him with my heart, and he helped me;
so my heart is full of joy,
and I will thank him with my song.

The voice of Yahweh is over the waters;
the God of glory thunders,
Yahweh, over many waters.

The voice of Yahweh makes the hinds to calve{d}
and strips the forests bare,
and in his temple everyone says, “Glory!”

In you, Yahweh, I have taken refuge;
let me never be ashamed;
deliver me in your righteousness.

I will be glad and rejoice in your covenant love,
for you have seen my affliction;
you have known the distresses of my soul,

Have pity on me, Yahweh, for I am in distress;
my eyes are worn out from sorrow,
and so are my soul and body.

For my life is spent with sorrow,
and my years with sighing;
my strength fails because of my iniquity,{c}
and my bones waste away.

Yahweh, let me not be ashamed, for I call upon you;
let the wicked be ashamed;
let them be silent in Sheol.

For day and night your hand was heavy upon me;
my moisture was turned into the drought of summer.{c}
Selah

You are my shelter;
you protect me from trouble;
you surround me with songs of rescue.
Selah

Let ruin come upon him when he does not know it;
let his own net that he has hidden catch him;
into that very ruin let him fall!

But as for me, when they were sick, my clothing was sackcloth;
I humbled my soul with fasting;
and my prayer returned into my own bosom.{c}

I walked around as if mourning a friend or brother;
I bent low in grief,
like someone weeping for his mother.

But in my limping they were glad and came together;
the smiters gathered against me,
and I did not know it;
they tore and did not cease;

Transgression speaks to the wicked
deep within his heart;{a}
there is no fear of God before his eyes.{b}

He devises mischief on his bed;
he sets himself on a way that is not good;
he does not reject evil.

Your righteousness is like the mountains of God;
your judgments are a great deep;
man and beast you preserve, Yahweh.

Be quiet before Yahweh and wait for him patiently;
do not be upset by people who succeed in their ways,
by those who carry out evil plans!

The wicked have drawn the sword and bent their bow
to bring down the poor and needy,
to slay those whose way is upright;

But the wicked shall perish;
and the enemies of Yahweh shall be as the glory of the pastures;{d}
they shall be consumed; into smoke they shall be consumed away.

For Yahweh loves justice;
he will not forsake his faithful ones.
They are preserved forever,{f}
but the children of the wicked shall be cut off.

Wait for Yahweh and keep his way,
and he will exalt you to inherit the land;
you will see it when the wicked are cut off.

And Yahweh shall help them and deliver them;
he shall deliver them from the wicked and save them,
because they trust in him.

Those who seek my life lay snares;
those who seek my hurt speak of ruin
and meditate on treachery all day long.

I was mute with silence;
I held my peace, to no avail,{b}
and my sorrow was stirred up.

My heart was hot inside me;
in my musing a fire was kindled;
then I spoke out with my tongue:

Surely every man walks about as a phantom;
surely they are in an uproar for nothing;
he heaps up riches and knows not who shall gather them.

“Hear my prayer, Yahweh,
and listen to my cry;
do not stay silent when I weep;
for I am a foreigner living with you,
a stranger like all my ancestors.

Many, Yahweh my God, are the wonders you have done,
and your thoughts toward us;
none can be set in order beside you;
if I would declare and speak of them,
they are more than can be numbered.

Sacrifice and offering you did not desire;
ears you have opened for me;{b}
burnt offering and sin offering
you have not required.

I have preached righteousness in the great congregation;
lo, I have not held back my lips,
Yahweh, you know.

I have not kept your righteousness hidden in my heart;
I have told of your faithfulness and rescue;
I have not kept your steadfast love and truth
secret from the great assembly.

For evils without number have compassed me about;
my iniquities have taken hold of me, so that I cannot look up;
they are more than the hairs of my head,
and my heart forsakes me.

But I am poor and needy;
yet the Lord thinks of me.
You are my help and my deliverer;
make no delay, O my God.

Yahweh will preserve him and keep him alive,
and he shall be blessed upon the earth;{a}
and you will not hand him over to the will of his enemies.

And if one comes to see me, he speaks emptiness;
his heart gathers iniquity to itself;
when he goes outside, he tells it.

Even my close friend, whom I trusted,
the one who shared my bread,
has raised his heel against me.{d}

Blessed be Yahweh, the God of Israel,
from everlasting to everlasting!
Amen and Amen.{e}

My tears have been my food by day and night,
while people keep asking me all day,
“Where is your God?”

O my God, my soul is bowed down within me;
therefore I remember you from the land of the Jordan
and of the Hermons, from Mount Mizar.{c}

Send out your light and your truth; let them lead me;
let them bring me to your holy mountain
and to your dwelling places!

With your hand you dispossessed the nations
and planted our fathers;
you brought harm on the peoples
and sent our fathers spreading out.{a}

My heart is stirred by a noble word;
I speak what I have composed for the king;
my tongue is the pen of a nimble writer.

You are the most handsome of men;
gracious words flow from your lips;
for this God has blessed you forever.

In your splendor, ride out in triumph
for the sake of truth, humility and justice;{c}
let your right hand show you fearsome deeds.

In robes of many colors she is brought to the king;
the maidens who follow her, her companions,
are brought in to you.

Yahweh of Armies is with us;
the God of Jacob is our high fortress.
Selah

He ends wars all over the earth;
he breaks bows and shatters spears;
he sets the wagons{b} on fire.

“Be still, and know that I am God.
I will be exalted among the nations;
I will be exalted in the earth!”

Yahweh of Armies is with us;
the God of Jacob is our high fortress.
Selah

The nobles of the peoples are gathered
as the people of the God of Abraham;
for the shields{c} of the earth belong to God;
he is highly exalted.

Majestic in height, the delight of the whole earth,
is Mount Zion, the remote heights of the north,{a}
the city of the great King.

Like your name, O God,
your praise extends to the ends of the earth;
righteousness fills your right hand.

mark well her ramparts;
pass through her citadels,
that you may tell it to the generation to come,

that this is God,
our God forever and ever.
He will guide us beyond death.{b}

Everyone can see that even the wise die;
fools and the senseless perish alike
and leave their riches to others.

Their tombs{d} are their houses forever,
their dwellings from generation to generation;
they call their lands by their own names.

Like sheep they are appointed for Sheol;
death shall shepherd them,
and the upright shall rule over them in the morning.
Their form shall waste away in Sheol,
far from any lofty dwelling.{e}

Our God comes and will not stay silent;
fire devours before him,
and round about him the storm rages.

“Listen, my people, and I will speak;
Israel, I will testify against you.
I am God, your God.

These things you did, and I held my peace;
you imagined I was altogether such a one as you.
But I will reprove you and set it all in order before your eyes.

He who brings thanksgiving as his offering gives me glory;
and to him who keeps to the right way
I will show the salvation of God!”

Be gracious to me, O God, according to your covenant love;
according to the greatness of your compassion
wipe away my transgressions.

You alone are the one I have sinned against;
I have done what is evil in your sight,
so you are right in what you say
and fair in your judgment.{b}

Then you will delight in right sacrifices,
in burnt offering and whole offering;
then bulls will be offered on your altar.

“See, here is the man who would not make God his stronghold,
but trusted in his great riches
and grew strong in his destruction!”{c}

I will give you thanks forever for what you have done;
I will wait on your name, for it is good,
in the presence of your faithful ones.

The fool has said in his heart, “There is no God.”
They are corrupt; they commit abominable injustice;
there is no one who does good.

Every one of them has turned back; together they have become rotten;
there is none who does good,
not even one.

They were terrified there,
although there was nothing to be afraid of!{b}
God has scattered the bones of those camped around you;
you put them to shame, because God has rejected them.

If only Israel’s rescue would come from Zion!
When God brings his people back from captivity,{c}
Jacob will celebrate and Israel will be glad.

For it was not an enemy who reproached me;
that I could endure;
it was not one who hated me who lifted himself against me;
from him I could have hidden.

Let death come upon them by surprise;
let them go down alive to Sheol!{b}
For evil is in their dwelling, in their very midst.

He has ransomed my soul in peace
from the war against me,
for many are against me.

In God I praise his word;
in God I have put my trust; I will not be afraid.
What can flesh do to me?

They band together; they lie in ambush;
they watch my heels,
as they have waited for my life.

You have tallied my wanderings;
place my tears in your flask.
Are they not recorded in your book?

Then shall my enemies be turned back
on the day I call;
this I know: God is on my side.

They spread a net for my feet;
my soul was bent low;
they dug a pit before me,
and into the middle of it they themselves have fallen.
Selah

Wake up, my glory!{b}
Wake up, lute and harp!
I will rouse the dawn!

For behold, they lie in wait for my life;
fierce men band together against me,
not for my transgression nor for my sin, Yahweh,

They come back at nightfall;
they snarl like a dog
and go all around the city.

Do not kill them, or my people may forget;
make them wander by your power and bring them down,
O Lord, our shield!

They come back at nightfall;
they snarl like a dog
and go all around the city.

O my Strength, to you I will make music,
for God is my high tower,
the God who shows me covenant love.

You have given a banner to those who fear you,
to be raised up because of the truth.{d}
Selah

God has spoken in his holiness:{f}
“I will exult; I will divide up Shechem
and measure out the Valley of Succoth.

Gilead is mine; Manasseh is mine;
Ephraim is the helmet on my head;
Judah is my scepter.

Moab is the basin I wash in;
over Edom I throw my sandal;{g}
over Philistia I raise my shout.”

Trust in him at every time, O people;
pour out your hearts before him;
God is a refuge for us.
Selah

Men of low birth are only a breath;
men of high birth are a lie;
put on the scales, they go up;
together they weigh less than a breath.

Put no trust in extortion;
set no vain hope on robbery;
if riches increase, do not set your heart on them.

Once God has spoken;
twice I have heard this:
that power belongs to God,

O God, you are my God; earnestly I search for you;
my soul is thirsty for you;
my body longs for you,
as in a parched and weary land where no water is.

But the king will celebrate in God;
all who take oaths in his name will exult,
while the mouths of liars are shut.

They strengthen themselves in an evil plan;
they talk of laying snares in secret;
they think, “Who will see them?”{a}

And all men will be afraid;
they will declare the work of God
and consider wisely what he has done.

You care for the land and give it water;
you make it very fertile;
God’s stream is full of water;
you supply grain for the people,
for this is how you prepare the soil.

the meadows put on flocks like a garment;
the valleys wrap themselves in grain;
they shout for joy; yes, they sing.

The whole earth worships you;
they sing to you;
they sing out your name.”
Selah

He turned the sea into dry ground;
they passed through the river on foot.{a}
There we rejoiced in him,

He rules forever by his might;
his eyes watch over the nations;
let the rebels not raise themselves up.{b}
Selah

you made men ride over our heads;
through fire and through water we went;
then you led us out into abundance.{c}

May God be gracious to us and bless us
and make his face shine upon us,{a}
Selah

As smoke is blown away, so blow them away;
as wax melts at the fire,
so let the wicked perish before God.

Sing to God; make music to his name;
build up a highway for him who rides through the deserts;{b}
Yah is his name;{c} exult before him.

God gives the lonely a home to live in;
he leads out the prisoners into prosperity,
but the rebellious live in a sun-scorched land.

the earth trembled; the heavens poured down
before the face of God, the One of Sinai,{d}
before the face of God, the God of Israel.

Even as you lie among the sheep pens,{g}
a dove’s wings are plated with silver,
her pinions with a greenish gleam of gold.

You went up to the height; you led captives captive;
you received gifts among men,
even among the rebellious, that Yah God might dwell there.{k}

There is little Benjamin, in front, ruling over them;
there are the leaders of Judah with their crowd,
the leaders of Zebulun and the leaders of Naphtali.

Rebuke the beast among the reeds,{o}
the herd of bulls with the calves of the peoples,
trampling those who delight in silver;{p}
scatter the peoples who take pleasure in war.

Kingdoms of the earth, sing to God;
make music to the Lord,
Selah

Ascribe power to God;
his splendor rests over Israel,
and his might is in the clouds.

You are awe-inspiring, God, in your sanctuary;
the God of Israel gives power and strength to his people.
Praise God!

There are more people who hate me for nothing{b}
than hairs on my head;
my attackers, my lying enemies, are strong.
Must I repay
what I never took?

Let none who wait for you be ashamed on my account,
Lord Yahweh of Armies;
let none who seek you be humiliated on my account,
O God of Israel.

Pull me out of the mud, and do not let me sink;
let me be rescued from those who hate me
and from the deep waters.

You know the insults I bear,
my shame and my dishonor;
all my adversaries are in your sight.

Insults have broken my heart, and I am sick;
I looked for pity, but there was none,
for comforters, but I found no one.

For God will save Zion
and rebuild the cities of Judah,
and they shall live there and possess it;

But I am afflicted and needy;
hurry to me, O God!
You are my help and the one who sets me free;
Yahweh, do not delay!

On you I have leaned from birth;
you are the one who brought me from my mother’s womb;{b}
my praise is always of you.

saying, “God has left him;
chase him and seize him,
for no one will rescue him.”

Let my accusers be shamed and consumed;
let those who seek my harm
be wrapped in insult and disgrace.

Your righteousness, O God, reaches the heights;
you have done great things;
O God, who is like you?

So may he live, and may Sheba’s gold be given him;
may they pray for him continually
and bless him all day long.

Let there be an abundance of grain in the land,
waving on the mountaintops;
let its fruit sway like Lebanon,
and let those of the city blossom like the grass of the earth.

May his name last forever;
may his fame{d} continue as long as the sun shines!
May every nation find blessing through him{e}
and call him fortunate!

May his glorious name be praised forever;
may his glory fill the whole earth!
Amen and amen!{f}

But as for me, nearness to God is my good;
I have made the Lord Yahweh my refuge,
that I may tell of all your works.

We do not see our signs;
there is no longer a prophet,
and none among us knows how long.

To you, O God, we give thanks, we give thanks;
and near is your name;{a}
they recount your wonderful works.

For Yahweh holds a cup in his hand;
the wine in it foams and is mixed with spices,
and he pours it out;

The stouthearted were stripped of their spoil;
they sank into their sleep;
none of the men of war could find their hands.

When I was in trouble I looked for the Lord;
at night I reached out my hand and did not grow tired;
my soul refused to be comforted.

I think of God, and I groan;
I ponder, and my spirit faints.
Selah

I call to mind my song in the night;
I muse with my heart,
and my spirit searches:

The waters saw you, O God;
the waters saw you and writhed;
the very deeps trembled.

The clouds poured down water;
the skies gave a thundering voice;
your arrows flashed back and forth.

Your thunder’s voice rolled in the whirlwind;
lightnings lit the world;
the earth trembled and shook.

that they might place their hope in God,
not forgetting the works of God,
but guarding his commands;

So when Yahweh heard, he was furious;
a fire was lit against Jacob,
and anger also rose against Israel,

the anger of God rose against them;
he killed the sturdiest of them
and struck down Israel’s young men.{g}

He leveled a road for his wrath;
he did not hold back their soul from death
but handed their life to pestilence.

He drove out nations before them;
he allotted them a heritage by measuring line
and settled the tribes of Israel in their tents.

O God, the nations have invaded your inheritance;
they have made your holy temple unclean;
they have turned Jerusalem into heaps of rubble.

Do not remember against us the sins of former days;{a}
let your mercies hurry to meet us,
for we are laid very low.

Let the groaning of the captive come before you;
by the greatness of your arm
spare those condemned to die.{b}

Then we, your people and the sheep you pasture,
will give you thanks forever;
to every generation we will tell your praise.

God of Armies, come back, we pray!
Look down from heaven and see;
take care of this vine,

He established it as a decree for Joseph
when he marched out against{c} the land of Egypt.
I heard a language I did not know:{d}

You called in trouble, and I rescued you;
I answered you from where the thunder hides;
I put you to the test at the waters of Meribah.{f}
Selah

They neither know nor understand;
they walk about in darkness;
all the foundations of the earth are shaken.

Assyria too has joined them;
they have become the strong arm{b} of the children of Lot.{c}
Selah

As they pass through the Valley of Baca,{b}
they make it a place of springs;
the early rain also wraps it in blessings.{c}

Yahweh God of Armies, hear my prayer;
give ear, O God of Jacob!
Selah

For Yahweh God is a sun and shield;
Yahweh bestows grace and glory;
he does not keep back any good thing
from those who walk with integrity.

You lifted the iniquity of your people;
all their sin you hid from view.
Selah

Let me hear what God, Yahweh, will say,
for he will speak peace to his people, to his faithful ones;
only let them not go back to foolishness.

Keep my soul, for I am faithful to you;{a}
save your servant, you who are my God,
the one who trusts in you.

Teach me your way, Yahweh,
that I may walk in your truth;
make my heart single to fear your name.

O God, insolent men have risen against me;
a gang of ruthless men seeks my life,
and they do not keep you before them.

Turn toward me and have mercy on me;
grant your strength to your servant,
and rescue the son of your handmaid.

You have taken my friends far from me;
you have made me loathsome to them.
I am shut in and cannot get out;

my eye wastes away because of affliction.
Every day I call to you, Yahweh;
I spread out my hands to you.

Yahweh God of Armies,
who is mighty as you are, O Yah?{c}
Your faithfulness is all around you.

Long ago you spoke by vision to your devoted ones{f} and said,
“I have given aid to a warrior;
I have exalted a man chosen out of the people.

You have cut short the days of his youth;
you have wrapped him in shame.
Selah

For a thousand years in your eyes
are like yesterday once it has gone by,
or like a watch in the night.{d}

Seventy years make up the days of our life,
or, given strength, eighty;{e}
yet the best of them{f} is labor and sorrow;
quickly it passes, and away we fly.

He will shelter you under his pinions;
under his wings you will take cover;
his faithfulness is shield and wall.

He will call on me, and I will answer him;
I will be with him in trouble;
I will rescue him and give him honor.

For look, your enemies, Yahweh,
for look, your enemies will perish;
all evildoers will be scattered.

Yahweh reigns;{a} he is robed in majesty;
Yahweh is robed; he has girded himself with strength.
Yes, the world is set firm; it will not be shaken.

The floods have lifted up, Yahweh,
the floods have lifted up their voice;
the floods lift up their pounding.

Your testimonies stand utterly firm;
holiness is fitting for your house,
Yahweh, for endless days.

He will turn back their own iniquity on them
and wipe them out for their evil;
Yahweh our God will wipe them out.

Say among the nations, “Yahweh reigns!
Yes, the world is set firm; it will not be shaken;
he will judge the peoples with fairness.”

Let all who serve carved images be put to shame,
who boast in worthless idols;
bow down to him, all you gods!{a}

Zion has heard and rejoiced;
the daughters of Judah are glad
because of your judgments, Yahweh.

You who love Yahweh, hate evil!
He guards the lives of his faithful ones;
he rescues them from the hand of the wicked.

Mighty is the King who loves justice.{b}
You have established fairness;
you have done justice and righteousness in Jacob.

Yahweh our God, you answered them;
you were a God who forgave them,
yet one who punished their misdeeds.

Know that Yahweh is God!
He made us, and we are his;{b}
we are his people, the sheep he pastures.

For Yahweh is good;
his covenant love lasts forever,
and his faithfulness through all generations.

You will rise and have compassion on Zion,
for it is time to show her favor;
the appointed time has come.

They will be destroyed, but you will last;
they will all wear out like a coat.
You will swap them like clothes,
and they will be gone;

He sets the frame of his upstairs rooms on the waters;
he takes the clouds as his chariot;
he travels on the wings of the wind;

How many are your works, Yahweh!
In wisdom you have made them all;
the earth is full of your creatures.

When you hide your face, they panic;
when you remove their breath, they die
and go back to dust.

so that they might keep his statutes
and observe his laws.
Hallelujah!{g}

Hallelujah!{a}
Give thanks to Yahweh, for he is good,
for his covenant love lasts forever!

Our fathers in Egypt
did not grasp your wonders;
they did not remember your abundant covenant love,
but rebelled at the sea, at the Red Sea.{b}

and gathered in from the lands,
from east and from west,
from north and from the sea.{b}

God has spoken in his holiness:{c}
“I will exult; I will divide up Shechem
and measure out the valley of Succoth.

Gilead is mine; Manasseh is mine;
Ephraim is the helmet on my head;
Judah is my scepter.

Moab is my washbasin;
on Edom I throw my sandal;
over Philistia I shout in triumph.”

For wicked and deceitful mouths
have opened against me;
they have spoken to me with lying tongues.

He dressed himself in cursing as in a robe;
may it enter his body like water,
and his bones like oil!

But you, Yahweh, my Lord,
deal with me for the sake of your name;
because your steadfast love is good, deliver me!

The declaration of Yahweh to my lord:{a}
“Sit at my right hand,
until I make your enemies a footstool for your feet.”

Yahweh has sworn and will not change his mind:
“You are a priest forever
after the order of Melchizedek.”{c}

He will execute judgment on the nations
and heap up the dead;
he will crush the head over a vast land.

Hallelujah!{a}
I will give thanks to Yahweh with my whole heart,
in the circle of the upright and in the assembly.

He sent redemption to his people;
he has ordained his covenant forever.
Holy and awesome is his name!

The fear of Yahweh is the beginning of wisdom;{b}
all who practice it have good insight.
His praise stands forever.

Hallelujah!{a}
Happy is the man who fears Yahweh,
who takes great delight in his commandments!

He has scattered his gifts; he has given to the poor;{b}
his righteousness stands forever;
his horn will be lifted high in honor.

The wicked sees it and is vexed;
he gnashes his teeth and wastes away;
what the wicked long for comes to nothing.

Hallelujah!{a}
Praise, you servants of Yahweh,
praise the name of Yahweh!

They have hands, yet no touch;
they have feet, yet they never walk;
no sound comes from their throat.

Yahweh has remembered us; he will bless—
he will bless the house of Israel;
he will bless the house of Aaron;

But we will bless Yah
from now on and forevermore.
Hallelujah!{b}

The cords of death wrapped around me;
the anguish of Sheol{a} found me;
I found distress and grief.

Yahweh, truly I am your servant;
I am your servant, the son of your maidservant.
You have loosed my bonds.

They surrounded me like bees;
they were extinguished like a fire of thorns;
in the name of Yahweh I cut them off!

where the tribes go up, the tribes of Yah,
as was decreed for Israel,{a}
to give thanks to the name of Yahweh.

It is useless to get up at dawn
and stay up into the night,
eating the bread of hard toil;
for to his beloved he gives sleep.{a}

Instead, I have made my soul calm and still,
like a child weaned from its mother’s milk;
my soul within me is like that child.

He brings up the mists from the far edges of the earth;
he forms lightning bolts to go with the rain
and draws the wind out of his treasuries.

I bow down toward your holy temple
and give thanks to your name
for your covenant love and your faithfulness,
for you have made your promise great, above all your name.{b}

to you even darkness is not dark;
night is as bright as day,
for darkness and light are alike to you.

I praise you, for I am made in an awe-inspiring and wonderful way.{c}
Wonderful are your works;
my soul knows it very well.

Your eyes saw me while I was yet unformed;
in your book were all recorded
the days fashioned for me,
when as yet there was not one of them.{d}

Keep me, Yahweh, from the hands of the wicked;
guard me from men of violence,
who plan to trip up my steps.

The proud have hidden a trap for me,
and ropes;
they have stretched out a net along the road;
they have laid traps for me. Selah

Do not grant, Yahweh, the desires of the wicked;
do not let his plot succeed,
or they will exalt themselves. Selah

Let burning coals fall on them!{a}
Let them be cast into the fire,
into pits, never to rise again!

Let a righteous person hit me—it is a kindness;
let him rebuke me—it is like oil on my head;
my head will not turn away from it.
But my prayer will always oppose the actions of the wicked.{a}

Look on my right side and see:
nobody pays any attention to me;
I have nowhere to flee;
no one cares about my life.

I cry to you, Yahweh;
I say, “You are my refuge,
my portion in the land of the living.”

Hear my prayer, Yahweh;
listen to my pleading!
Answer me in your faithfulness and in your righteousness!

For the enemy has hunted my soul;
he has beaten my life down into the dust;
he has made me dwell in darkness like the long dead.

I call to mind the days of old;
I reflect on all your deeds;
I muse on what your hands have made.

Blessed be Yahweh, my rock,
who trains my hands for war,
my fingers for battle;

Stretch out your hands from on high;
set me free and rescue me from the great waters,
from the hand of foreigners,

may our barns be full,
supplying produce of every kind;
may our flocks bring forth thousands,
tens of thousands in our fields;

may our oxen be laden;{c}
may no wall be breached and no one led captive,
and no wailing be heard in our streets!

the Maker of heaven and earth,
the sea, and all that is in them,
who keeps faith forever;

who executes justice for the oppressed,
who gives food to the hungry.
Yahweh sets the prisoners free;

Yahweh opens the eyes of the blind;
Yahweh raises up those who are bowed down;
Yahweh loves the righteous;

Yahweh watches over the sojourners;
he upholds the fatherless and the widow,
but the way of the wicked he turns upside down.

Hallelujah!
For it is good to sing praises to our God;
for it is pleasant, and praise is fitting.{a}

He wraps the sky in clouds;
he readies rain for the earth;
he makes the hills sprout grass.

He has not dealt this way with any other nation;
they do not know his rules.
Hallelujah!

Hallelujah!
Praise Yahweh from the heavens;
praise him in the heights!

Let them praise the name of Yahweh,
for his name alone is exalted;
his majesty is above earth and heaven.

Hallelujah!
Praise God in his sanctuary;
praise him in his mighty expanse!{a}
